problem:
11. Given that the internal angles $A, B, C$ of $\triangle ABC$ have opposite sides $a, b, c$ respectively, and $\sqrt{3} b \cos \frac{A+B}{2}=c \sin B$.
(1) Find the size of $\angle C$;
(2) If $a+b=\sqrt{3} c$, find $\sin A$.

